  "as_of": "2022-09-28",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would revise how Animal Health Australia and Plant Health Australia receive and use industry levies, including funding for emergency biosecurity responses.",
   "It would allow animal health funding priorities to cover additional emergency response deeds and broaden permitted plant levy spending to include maintaining or promoting plant health.",
   "The amendments would begin after royal assent, replacing redundant funding arrangements and allowing departmental determinations to identify the industry bodies representing particular plant products."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "Animal health legislation would gain a regulation-making power to prescribe additional eligible response deeds.",
   "Obsolete honey levy provisions in animal health legislation would be repealed.",
   "Plant Health Australia would receive total relevant levy receipts instead of excess amounts being redirected through the research funding mechanism."
  ],
  "affected": "Animal and plant industry levy payers, industry representative bodies, the two health organisations and Commonwealth administrators would be affected.",
